    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 606 of 2006",
    "lawSection": "Volunteer Firefighters' Benefit Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7852\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 606 of the laws of 2006 amending the volunteer\nfirefighters' benefit law relating to creating a presumption relating to\ncertain lung disabilities incurred by volunteer firefighters, in\nrelation to the effectiveness of such chapter\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would extend, until June 30, 2020, section 11-c of\nvolunteer firefighters' benefit law, which governs benefits for the\ndeath or disability of volunteer firefighters due to lung disease.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill extends the presumption related to disability\nbenefits for death or disability related to lung disease in volunteer\nfirefighters for an additional five years, until June 30, 2030.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVolunteer firefighters too often suffer injuries or death relating to\nlung disease in the line of duty. As a result, the legislature estab-\nlished specific procedures to expedite the handling of such claims. This\nlegislation extends the provisions relating to disability due to lung\ndisease until June 30, 2030.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter 58 of the laws of 2020 (PPGG Part XXX subpart B item BB)\n\nChapter 25 of the laws of 2015\n\nChapter 282 of the laws of 2010\n\nChapter 120 of the Laws of 2008\n\nChapter 606 of the Laws of 2006\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNote.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis. act shall take effect immediately\n",
